Z||000000||fierospeeder||12-04-1999||01:56 AM||||After finishing my oil pan project, im pretty sure its a success because i dont see it leaking.  But now i notice a red drip and discovered the trans line has a crack in it probably of me lifting the engine up with a hoist.  It is the rubber lines with the hose clamp on it.  I was wondering if GM still sells these and whats the est price.  ||||reg||13
Z||000001||batboy||12-04-1999||02:34 AM||||If GM no longer stocks them, do not use fuel line hose or something like that as a substitute. It won't last long. You should be able to find some appropriate high pressure hose the right size from a shop that does hydraulic work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-04-1999||12:07 PM||||line stock for the tranny is available at most any autoparts shop. it may even be out on the shelf with the aftermarket transmission cooler stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||12-05-1999||01:38 PM||||My coolant lines were F.U.B.A.R when I got my fiero.  Ogre is right, I bought "transmission coolant lines" from the autopart store.  They just ask you how much you need.  It was pretty reasonable... And no leaks!||||reg||1
